# What the item prompt takes for an ID: item 2 of the item list
# installed with Install in.  5150, digits naming no item, is searched as text
# and lists item 1, whose model it is; Esc goes back to the prompt with
# its title; 0, which the server refuses as an ID, is searched as text
# and lists the items holding a 0; nine digits, more than an ID holds,
# are text too and find nothing; eight digits with blanks around them
# are item 1's ID.
T ADMIN
K ENTER
T Retro1986
K ENTER
K ALT-I
T I
K DOWN ALT-C I
T 5150
K ENTER
S PICKNUM
K ESC
S ASKNUM
K CTRL-Y
T 0
K ENTER
S PICKZERO
K ESC CTRL-Y
T 000000001
K ENTER
S PICK9
K ESC CTRL-Y SPACE
T 00000001
K SPACE ENTER
S INSTALL
K F3
T Y
